5. Gradually blend in flour mixture.
6. Roll dough into walnut-sized balls.
7. Place on ungreased baking sheets.
8. Flatten with fork in crisscross pattern.
9. Bake 10-12 min until lightly golden.
10. Cool on baking sheet for 2 min before removing.', 'cookies', 'https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1670938559598-135dfaabe8e5?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MTd8fG9hdG1lYWwlMjByYWlzaW4lMjBjb29raWVzfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Gingerbread Cookies', ARRAY['3 cups plain flour', '2 tsp ground ginger', '1 tsp baking soda', '1 tsp ground cinnamon', '1/2 tsp ground cloves', '1/2 tsp salt', '3/4 cup butter, softened', '1 cup brown sugar', '1/2 cup molasses', '1 large egg', 'Royal icing for decorating'], '1. Mix flour, ginger, baking soda, cinnamon, cloves, and salt.
2. Cream butter and brown sugar until fluffy.
3. Beat in molasses and egg.
4. Gradually mix in flour mixture.
5. Divide dough in half, wrap in plastic, chill 2 hours.
6. Preheat oven to 180°C.
7. Roll dough to 6mm thickness on floured surface.
8. Cut with cookie cutters, place on lined baking sheets.
9. Bake 8-10 min until edges are lightly browned.
10. Cool completely before decorating with royal icing.', 'cookies', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1610562275255-03b7fa0d4655?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8NHx8Z2luZ2VyYnJlYWQlMjBjb29raWVzfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Shortbread Cookies', ARRAY['2 cups plain flour', '1/2 tsp salt', '1 cup butter, softened', '2/3 cup powdered sugar', '1 tsp vanilla extract'], '1. Preheat oven to 160°C.
2. Mix flour and salt in a bowl.
3. Cream butter and powdered sugar until light and fluffy.
4. Beat in vanilla extract.
5. Gradually mix in flour mixture until just combined.
6. Press dough into ungreased 23cm round pan.
7. Score into 16 wedges with knife.
8. Prick all over with fork.
9. Bake 25-30 min until lightly golden.
10. Cut along score lines while warm, cool in pan.', 'cookies', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1691201327097-3d62e5c7b75f?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MTZ8fHNob3J0YnJlYWQlMjBjb29raWVzfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Lemon Crinkle Cookies', ARRAY['2 1/4 cups plain flour', '1/2 tsp baking soda', '1/2 tsp salt', '1/2 cup butter, softened', '1 cup granulated sugar', '1 large egg', '2 tbsp lemon zest', '2 tbsp fresh lemon juice', '1/2 tsp vanilla extract', 'Powdered sugar for rolling'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix flour, baking soda, and salt.
3. Cream butter and granulated sugar until fluffy.
4. Beat in egg, lemon zest, lemon juice, and vanilla.
5. Gradually mix in flour mixture.
6. Chill dough for 30 min.
7. Roll dough into walnut-sized balls.
8. Roll each ball in powdered sugar.
9. Place on prepared baking sheets.
10. Bake 10-12 min until edges are lightly golden.', 'cookies', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565958011703-44f9829ba187?w=400', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Thumbprint Cookies', ARRAY['2 cups plain flour', '1/2 tsp salt', '1 cup butter, softened', '2/3 cup brown sugar', '2 large egg yolks', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '2 large egg whites, lightly beaten', '1 1/2 cups finely chopped walnuts', '1/3 cup jam or preserves'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix flour and salt in a bowl.
3. Cream butter and brown sugar until fluffy.
4. Beat in egg yolks and vanilla.
5. Gradually mix in flour mixture.
6. Roll dough into walnut-sized balls.
7. Dip each ball in beaten egg whites, then roll in chopped nuts.
8. Place on prepared baking sheets.
9. Make indentation in center with thumb.
10. Fill each indentation with 1/2 tsp jam.
11. Bake 15-18 min until lightly golden.', 'cookies', 'https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1671399556279-a681f8668992?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MXx8dGh1bWJwcmludCUyMGNvb2tpZXN8ZW58MHx8MHx8fDA%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Chocolate Crinkle Cookies', ARRAY['1 cup plain flour', '1/2 cup unsweetened cocoa powder', '1 tsp baking powder', '1/4 tsp salt', '1 1/2 cups granulated sugar', '1/2 cup vegetable oil', '2 large eggs', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/2 cup powdered sugar for rolling'], '1. Mix flour, cocoa powder, baking powder, and salt.
2. Beat granulated sugar and oil until combined.
3. Beat in eggs one at a time, then vanilla.
4. Gradually mix in flour mixture.
5. Cover and chill dough for at least 4 hours.
6. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
7. Roll chilled dough into walnut-sized balls.
8. Roll each ball in powdered sugar until completely coated.
9. Place on prepared baking sheets.
10. Bake 10-12 min until cookies are cracked and set.', 'cookies', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1595447966838-4539afd86068?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8NHx8Y2hvY29sYXRlJTIwY2hyaW5rbGUlMjBjb29raWVzfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Chocolate Chip Cookies', ARRAY['2 1/4 cups almond flour', '1/2 tsp baking soda', '1/2 tsp salt', '1/2 cup coconut oil, melted', '1/2 cup erythritol sweetener', '1/4 cup sugar-free maple syrup', '2 large eggs', '2 tsp vanilla extract', '3/4 cup sugar-free chocolate chips'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix almond flour, baking soda, and salt in a bowl.
3. In another bowl, whisk melted coconut oil and erythritol.
4. Add maple syrup, eggs, and vanilla, mix well.
5. Gradually fold in flour mixture until just combined.
6. Stir in sugar-free chocolate chips.
7. Drop rounded tablespoons onto prepared baking sheets.
8. Bake 10-12 min until edges are lightly golden.
9. Cool on baking sheet for 5 min before removing.', 'sugar-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1709722487/photo/homemade-chocolate-chip-cookies.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=uXCdWJNjRx25YThGfUEIg7lUW2gm2LrWOvpRo1xj5Yk=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Brownies', ARRAY['1/2 cup almond flour', '1/4 cup unsweetened cocoa powder', '1/2 cup erythritol sweetener', '1/4 tsp salt', '1/3 cup coconut oil, melted', '2 large eggs', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/4 cup sugar-free chocolate chips', '1/4 cup chopped walnuts (optional)'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line 20cm square pan with parchment.
2. Mix almond flour, cocoa powder, erythritol, and salt.
3. In another bowl, whisk melted coconut oil, eggs, and vanilla.
4. Pour wet ingredients into dry ingredients, mix until smooth.
5. Fold in chocolate chips and walnuts if using.
6. Pour batter into prepared pan and smooth top.
7. Bake 20-25 min until toothpick has few moist crumbs.
8. Cool completely before cutting into squares.
9. Store covered for up to 5 days.', 'sugar-free', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515037893149-de7f840978e2?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8YnJvd25pZXN8ZW58MHx8MHx8fDA%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Banana Muffins', ARRAY['2 cups almond flour', '1 tsp baking soda', '1/2 tsp salt', '1 tsp cinnamon', '3 ripe bananas, mashed', '3 large eggs', '1/4 cup coconut oil, melted', '1/4 cup sugar-free maple syrup', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/2 cup chopped walnuts (optional)'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line muffin tin with paper cases.
2. Mix almond flour, baking soda, salt, and cinnamon.
3. In another bowl, mash bananas until smooth.
4. Add eggs, melted coconut oil, maple syrup, and vanilla to bananas.
5. Pour wet ingredients into dry ingredients, mix until just combined.
6. Fold in walnuts if using.
7. Fill muffin cases 3/4 full.
8. Bake 18-22 min until toothpick comes out clean.
9. Cool in pan for 5 min before removing.', 'sugar-free', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1616177337300-c8d69da312e8?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8M3x8YmFuYW5hJTIwbXVmZmlufGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Cinnamon Mousse', ARRAY['2 ripe avocados', '1/4 cup unsweetened cocoa powder', '1/4 cup powdered erythritol', '1/4 cup coconut milk', '2 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt', 'Fresh berries for garnish', 'Sugar-free whipped cream (optional)'], '1. Cut avocados in half, remove pits, and scoop out flesh.
2. Blend avocados in food processor until completely smooth.
3. Add cocoa powder, erythritol, coconut milk, vanilla, and salt.
4. Blend until smooth and creamy, scraping sides as needed.
5. Taste and adjust sweetness if needed.
6. Divide among serving glasses.
7. Chill for at least 2 h until set.
8. Garnish with berries and whipped cream before serving.
9. Best consumed within 24 h.', 'sugar-free', 'https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1669880504277-1c79daa58c12?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MTN8fG1vdXNzZXxlbnwwfHwwfHx8MA%3D%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Lemon Bars', ARRAY['Crust: 1 1/2 cups almond flour', '1/4 cup powdered erythritol', '1/4 tsp salt', '1/4 cup coconut oil, melted', 'Filling: 4 large eggs', '1/2 cup powdered erythritol', '1/3 cup fresh lemon juice', '2 tbsp lemon zest', '2 tbsp almond flour'], '1. Preheat oven to 160°C. Line 20cm square pan with parchment.
2. Mix almond flour, erythritol, and salt for crust.
3. Stir in melted coconut oil until mixture holds together.
4. Press into prepared pan and bake 15 min until golden.
5. Whisk eggs and erythritol until smooth.
6. Add lemon juice, zest, and almond flour.
7. Pour over hot crust and bake 20-25 min until set.
8. Cool completely before cutting into bars.
9. Dust with additional erythritol if desired.', 'sugar-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/505142371/photo/luscious-bliss-lemon-bars.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=Gcd-KZwaK5rgq700xk-2eNGDyCW5ysCeUoUxmvyorLQ=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Peanut Butter Cookies', ARRAY['1 cup natural peanut butter (no sugar added)', '1/2 cup erythritol sweetener', '1 large egg', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/2 tsp baking soda', '1/4 tsp salt'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix peanut butter and erythritol until smooth.
3. Beat in egg and vanilla extract.
4. Stir in baking soda and salt until combined.
5. Roll dough into 24 walnut-sized balls.
6. Place on prepared baking sheets.
7. Flatten with fork in crisscross pattern.
8. Bake 10-12 min until edges are lightly golden.
9. Cool on baking sheet for 5 min before removing.', 'sugar-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/609044534/photo/sea-salt-peanut-butter-cookies-with-milk.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=U_A01fyy7WiqmhtONHCnt8Qzlx7jmd583AuN7uJ_6vc=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Chia Pudding', ARRAY['1/4 cup chia seeds', '1 cup unsweetened almond milk', '2 tbsp sugar-free maple syrup', '1/2 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt', 'Fresh berries for topping', 'Chopped nuts for topping', 'Unsweetened coconut flakes'], '1. Whisk chia seeds, almond milk, maple syrup, vanilla, and salt.
2. Let sit for 5 min, then whisk again to prevent clumping.
3. Cover and refrigerate for at least 4 h or overnight.
4. Stir well before serving.
5. Divide between serving glasses.
6. Top with fresh berries, nuts, and coconut flakes.
7. Serve chilled.
8. Keeps in refrigerator for up to 5 days.', 'sugar-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1138253386/photo/chia-pudding-in-glass-jar-with-almond-milk-and-mango-on-white-background.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=uQndBPZxjXtatZZ3VsDFZWp3B9Xmq2bl0x5fZtcaGFA=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Apple Crisp', ARRAY['Filling: 6 large apples, peeled and sliced', '1/4 cup erythritol sweetener', '2 tbsp almond flour', '1 tsp cinnamon', '1/4 tsp nutmeg', 'Topping: 1 cup almond flour', '1/2 cup chopped almonds', '1/3 cup erythritol sweetener', '1/4 cup coconut oil, cold', '1/2 tsp cinnamon'], '1. Preheat oven to 190°C. Grease 23x33cm baking dish.
2. Toss sliced apples with erythritol, almond flour, cinnamon, and nutmeg.
3. Place apple mixture in prepared baking dish.
4. Mix almond flour, chopped almonds, erythritol, and cinnamon.
5. Cut in cold coconut oil until mixture resembles coarse crumbs.
6. Sprinkle topping evenly over apples.
7. Bake 30-35 min until topping is golden and apples are tender.
8. Cool for 10 min before serving.
9. Serve warm if desired.', 'sugar-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/175227596/photo/close-up-of-apple-crisps-in-a-white-bowl-and-a-single-spoon.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=-s1ZAAwvezOAOuCiXBr7lTCUnJtVxBSKzxUaQC4Uivk=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Chocolate Cake', ARRAY['1 3/4 cups almond flour', '3/4 cup unsweetened cocoa powder', '3/4 cup erythritol sweetener', '2 tsp baking powder', '1 tsp baking soda', '1/2 tsp salt', '2 large eggs', '1 cup unsweetened almond milk', '1/2 cup sugar-free applesauce', '1/3 cup coconut oil, melted', '2 tsp vanilla extract'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Grease 23cm round cake pan.
2. Mix almond flour, cocoa powder, erythritol, baking powder, baking soda, and salt.
3. In another bowl, whisk eggs, almond milk, applesauce, melted coconut oil, and vanilla.
4. Pour wet ingredients into dry ingredients, mix until smooth.
5. Pour batter into prepared pan.
6. Bake 30-35 min until toothpick comes out clean.
7. Cool in pan for 10 min.
8. Turn out onto wire rack to cool completely.
9. Frost with sugar-free frosting if desired.', 'sugar-free', 'https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1723867522131-af9733323bc1?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MXx8Y2hvY29sYXRlJTIwZnJlbmNoJTIwY2FrZXxlbnwwfHwwfHx8MA%3D%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Sugar-Free Energy Bites', ARRAY['1 cup old-fashioned oats', '1/2 cup natural almond butter', '1/3 cup sugar-free mini chocolate chips', '1/3 cup ground flaxseed', '1/4 cup chia seeds', '1/4 cup sugar-free maple syrup', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/4 tsp salt'], '1. Mix all ingredients in a large bowl until well combined.
2. If mixture is too dry, add 1-2 tbsp water.
3. If mixture is too wet, add more oats.
4. Cover and refrigerate for 30 min.
5. Roll mixture into 20 walnut-sized balls.
6. Store in refrigerator for up to 1 week.
7. Can be frozen for up to 3 months.
8. Let thaw for 5 min if frozen before eating.
9. Perfect grab-and-go healthy treat.', 'sugar-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/636970604/photo/energy-granola-bites.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=QRJoaB9vx3zr60jnIavQ0z2jwLKuicmaVb0dpwHUtGE=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Flourless Chocolate Cookies', ARRAY['2 cups powdered sugar', '3/4 cup unsweetened cocoa powder', '1/4 tsp salt', '3 large egg whites', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1 cup chocolate chips', '1/2 cup chopped walnuts (optional)'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line baking sheets with parchment paper.
2. Whisk together powdered sugar, cocoa powder, and salt.
3. In another bowl, whisk egg whites until foamy.
4. Add vanilla to egg whites.
5. Fold dry ingredients into egg whites until just combined.
6. Stir in chocolate chips and nuts if using.
7. Drop spoonfuls onto prepared baking sheets.
8. Bake for 10-12 min until tops are cracked and shiny.
9. Cool on baking sheet for 5 min before removing.', 'gluten-free', 'https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1670895801135-858a7d167ea4?q=80&w=1587&auto=format&fit=crop&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Almond Flour Lemon Bars', ARRAY['Crust: 2 cups almond flour', '1/4 cup powdered sugar', '1/4 tsp salt', '1/4 cup melted coconut oil', 'Filling: 4 large eggs', '3/4 cup granulated sugar', '1/3 cup fresh lemon juice', '2 tbsp lemon zest', '2 tbsp almond flour', 'Powdered sugar for dusting'], '1. Preheat oven to 160°C. Line 20cm square pan with parchment.
2. Mix almond flour, powdered sugar, and salt for crust.
3. Stir in melted coconut oil until mixture holds together.
4. Press into prepared pan and bake 15 min until golden.
5. Whisk eggs and granulated sugar until smooth.
6. Add lemon juice, zest, and almond flour.
7. Pour over hot crust and bake 20-25 min until set.
8. Cool completely before dusting with powdered sugar.
9. Cut into bars and serve.', 'gluten-free', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565958011703-44f9829ba187?w=400', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Coconut Macaroons', ARRAY['4 cups unsweetened shredded coconut', '4 large egg whites', '2/3 cup caster sugar', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/4 tsp salt', '200g dark chocolate, melted (optional)', '1 tbsp coconut oil (optional)'], '1. Preheat oven to 160°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix coconut, egg whites, sugar, vanilla, and salt.
3. Let mixture sit for 5 min to absorb moisture.
4. Using hands or ice cream scoop, form into mounds.
5. Place on prepared baking sheets, spacing 2cm apart.
6. Bake 20-25 min until golden brown.
7. Cool completely on baking sheets.
8. If desired, melt chocolate with coconut oil.
9. Dip bottom of cooled macaroons in chocolate, let set.', 'gluten-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1805087335/photo/white-macaron-shell.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=170jHFKohmNP66BLUHbynxtCdBwmIURerfFoVYCi69I=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Rice Flour Vanilla Cupcakes', ARRAY['1 1/2 cups rice flour', '1/2 cup potato starch', '1/4 cup tapioca flour', '1 tsp xanthan gum', '1 1/2 tsp baking powder', '1/2 tsp salt', '1/2 cup butter, softened', '3/4 cup caster sugar', '2 large eggs', '2 tsp vanilla extract', '3/4 cup milk'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line muffin tin with paper cases.
2. Whisk together rice flour, potato starch, tapioca flour, xanthan gum, baking powder, and salt.
3. Cream butter and sugar until light and fluffy.
4. Beat in eggs one at a time, then vanilla.
5. Alternately add dry ingredients and milk, beginning and ending with flour mixture.
6. Fill cupcake cases 2/3 full.
7. Bake 18-20 min until toothpick comes out clean.
8. Cool completely before frosting.
9. Top with vanilla buttercream or cream cheese frosting.', 'gluten-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1419282451/photo/vanilla-cupcakes-close-up-on-white-background.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=pRhw_loXxO2tG86iBN3hH5eXaRh_GVRZ1IL7QU79PIM=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Peanut Butter Energy Balls', ARRAY['1 cup old-fashioned oats (certified gluten-free)', '1/2 cup natural peanut butter', '1/3 cup honey', '1/3 cup mini chocolate chips', '1/3 cup ground flaxseed', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '2 tbsp chia seeds', '1/4 tsp salt'], '1. Mix all ingredients in a large bowl until well combined.
2. Cover and refrigerate for 30 min.
3. Roll mixture into 20 small balls using your hands.
4. Store in refrigerator for up to 1 week.
5. Serve chilled.
6. Optional: roll in shredded coconut or chopped nuts.
7. Can be frozen for up to 3 months.
8. Let thaw for 5 min before eating if frozen.', 'gluten-free', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1178621382/photo/cocoa-and-oat-energy-balls.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=neVXOXjAkDntr19xRknmeRTEfrDC1ILUluVHuhy-nkg=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Flourless Peanut Butter Cookies', ARRAY['1 cup natural peanut butter', '3/4 cup brown sugar', '1 large egg', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/2 tsp baking soda', '1/4 tsp salt', '1/2 cup chocolate chips (optional)'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix peanut butter and brown sugar until smooth.
3. Beat in egg and vanilla extract.
4. Stir in baking soda and salt until combined.
5. Fold in chocolate chips if using.
6. Roll dough into 24 balls and place on baking sheets.
7. Flatten with fork in crisscross pattern.
8. Bake 10-12 min until edges are lightly golden.
9. Cool on baking sheet for 5 min before removing.', 'gluten-free', 'https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1699372281288-14a43e77fec2?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cGVhbnV0JTIwYnV0dGVyJTIwY29va2llc3xlbnwwfHwwfHx8MA%3D%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Gluten-Free Brownies', ARRAY['1/2 cup almond flour', '1/4 cup cocoa powder', '1/2 tsp baking powder', '1/4 tsp salt', '1/2 cup coconut oil, melted', '3/4 cup coconut sugar', '2 large eggs', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/2 cup dark chocolate chips', '1/4 cup chopped walnuts (optional)'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line 20cm square pan with parchment.
2. Whisk almond flour, cocoa powder, baking powder, and salt.
3. In another bowl, mix melted coconut oil and coconut sugar.
4. Beat in eggs and vanilla until smooth.
5. Fold in dry ingredients until just combined.
6. Stir in chocolate chips and nuts if using.
7. Pour into prepared pan and smooth top.
8. Bake 25-30 min until toothpick has few moist crumbs.
9. Cool completely before cutting.', 'gluten-free', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1606313564200-e75d5e30476c?w=400', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Chia Seed Pudding', ARRAY['1/4 cup chia seeds', '1 cup coconut milk', '2 tbsp maple syrup', '1/2 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt', 'Fresh berries for topping', 'Chopped nuts for topping', 'Shredded coconut for topping'], '1. Whisk chia seeds, coconut milk, maple syrup, vanilla, and salt.
2. Let sit for 5 min, then whisk again to prevent clumping.
3. Cover and refrigerate for at least 4 h or overnight.
4. Stir before serving.
5. Divide between serving glasses or bowls.
6. Top with fresh berries, nuts, and coconut.
7. Serve chilled.
8. Keeps in refrigerator for up to 5 days.', 'gluten-free', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1591090909710-b6151c0d3d68?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8Y2hpYSUyMHB1ZGRpbmd8ZW58MHx8MHx8fDA%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Oat Flour Banana Muffins', ARRAY['2 cups oat flour (or ground oats)', '1 tsp baking soda', '1/2 tsp salt', '1 tsp cinnamon', '3 ripe bananas, mashed', '1/3 cup melted coconut oil', '1/2 cup honey', '2 large eggs', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/4 cup milk', '1/2 cup chocolate chips (optional)'], '1. Preheat oven to 180°C. Line muffin tin with paper cases.
2. Whisk oat flour, baking soda, salt, and cinnamon.
3. In another bowl, mash bananas until smooth.
4. Stir in melted coconut oil, honey, eggs, vanilla, and milk.
5. Fold wet ingredients into dry ingredients until just combined.
6. Stir in chocolate chips if using.
7. Fill muffin cases 3/4 full.
8. Bake 18-22 min until toothpick comes out clean.
9. Cool in pan for 5 min before removing.', 'gluten-free', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1587668178277-295251f900ce?w=400', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Coconut Flour Lemon Cake', ARRAY['3/4 cup coconut flour', '1/2 tsp baking soda', '1/2 tsp salt', '6 large eggs', '1/2 cup honey', '1/2 cup coconut oil, melted', '1/4 cup fresh lemon juice', '2 tbsp lemon zest', '1 tsp vanilla extract', 'Glaze: 1 cup powdered sugar', '3 tbsp lemon juice'], '1. Preheat oven to 160°C. Grease 23cm round cake pan.
2. Whisk coconut flour, baking soda, and salt.
3. Beat eggs and honey until light and fluffy.
4. Mix in melted coconut oil, lemon juice, zest, and vanilla.
5. Fold in dry ingredients until smooth.
6. Pour into prepared pan.
7. Bake 35-40 min until golden and toothpick comes out clean.
8. Cool completely in pan.
9. Mix powdered sugar and lemon juice for glaze.
10. Drizzle over cooled cake before serving.', 'gluten-free', 'https://plus.unsplash.com/premium_photo-1716918179075-d81daab96c4e?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8OXx8bGVtb24lMjBjYWtlfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Classic Vanilla Ice Cream', ARRAY['2 cups heavy cream', '1 cup whole milk', '3/4 cup granulated sugar', '6 large egg yolks', '2 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt'], '1. Heat cream and milk in a saucepan until just simmering.
2. Whisk egg yolks and sugar until pale and thick.
3. Slowly pour hot cream into yolks, whisking constantly.
4. Return mixture to saucepan and cook over low heat, stirring constantly.
5. Cook until mixture coats the back of a spoon (170°F).
6. Remove from heat, stir in vanilla and salt.
7. Strain through fine-mesh sieve and cool completely.
8. Churn in ice cream maker according to manufacturer instructions.
9. Transfer to container and freeze for at least 4 h.', 'frozen', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1549395156-e0c1fe6fc7a5?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8M3x8dmFuaWxsYSUyMGljZWNyZWFtfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Strawberry Popsicles', ARRAY['500g fresh strawberries, hulled', '1/2 cup granulated sugar', '2 tbsp fresh lemon juice', '1/4 cup water', '1 tbsp honey (optional)'], '1. Blend strawberries, sugar, lemon juice, water, and honey until smooth.
2. Strain mixture if you want smooth popsicles (optional).
3. Taste and adjust sweetness if needed.
4. Pour mixture into popsicle molds, leaving 1cm space at top.
5. Insert popsicle sticks.
6. Freeze for at least 6 h or overnight.
7. To remove, run warm water over outside of molds.
8. Store in freezer for up to 3 months.', 'frozen', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/685817724/photo/strawberry-and-raspberry-popsicles.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=_nHXeDcxu4yM1A-9DpdxSGxYp0nNGl2EkZhPD8qqeOY=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Strawberry Gelato', ARRAY['2 cups whole milk', '1/2 cup heavy cream', '3/4 cup granulated sugar', '5 large egg yolks', '200g strawberries, hulled and chopped', '1 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt'], '1. Heat milk and cream in a saucepan until steaming.
2. Whisk egg yolks, sugar until smooth.
3. Slowly add hot milk mixture to egg mixture, whisking constantly.
4. Return to saucepan and cook over medium-low heat, stirring constantly.
5. Cook until mixture coats spoon and reaches 170°F.
6. Remove from heat, add chopped strawberries, stir until melted.
7. Add vanilla and salt, strain through fine-mesh sieve.
8. Cool completely, then churn in ice cream maker.
9. Freeze for at least 4 h before serving.', 'frozen', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1621096229451-38ce90f1035c?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MTR8fGdlbGF0b3xlbnwwfHwwfHx8MA%3D%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Mango Sorbet', ARRAY['4 large ripe mangoes, peeled and chopped', '3/4 cup granulated sugar', '1/2 cup water', '3 tbsp fresh lime juice', '1 tbsp lime zest', 'Pinch of salt'], '1. Make simple syrup by boiling water and sugar until sugar dissolves.
2. Cool syrup completely.
3. Puree mangoes in blender until completely smooth.
4. Add cooled syrup, lime juice, lime zest, and salt to mango puree.
5. Blend until well combined.
6. Strain mixture through fine-mesh sieve if desired.
7. Churn in ice cream maker according to manufacturer instructions.
8. Transfer to container and freeze for at least 4 h.
9. Let soften 5-10 min before serving.', 'frozen', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1325470251/photo/yellow-ice-cream-sorbet-in-blue-ceramic-bowl-closeup.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=kEo9iJ601zTwhXJpFAJ-uiRA3zQ0L6AQVn4DPn18VpA=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Ice Cream Sandwiches', ARRAY['Cookies: 2 1/4 cups plain flour', '1 tsp baking soda', '1 tsp salt', '1 cup butter, softened', '3/4 cup brown sugar', '1/2 cup granulated sugar', '2 large eggs', '2 tsp vanilla extract', '2 cups chocolate chips', 'Filling: 1 liter vanilla ice cream, softened'], '1. Preheat oven to 190°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix flour, baking soda, and salt in a bowl.
3. Cream butter and both sugars until fluffy.
4. Beat in eggs and vanilla.
5. Gradually mix in flour mixture, then chocolate chips.
6. Drop large spoonfuls onto baking sheets, flatten slightly.
7. Bake 10-12 min until golden. Cool completely.
8. Spread softened ice cream on flat side of one cookie.
9. Top with another cookie, press gently.
10. Wrap in plastic and freeze for 2 h before serving.', 'frozen', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/481742880/photo/chocolate-chip-ice-cream-cookie-sandwiches.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=enX7zwbLJnoaTu_zpHpHB-9kgMhzbXqvzjFIKe2MQ2E=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Frozen Yogurt Bark', ARRAY['2 cups Greek yogurt', '3 tbsp honey', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/2 cup mixed berries', '1/4 cup chopped nuts', '2 tbsp mini chocolate chips', '1 tbsp chia seeds (optional)'], '1. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper.
2. Mix Greek yogurt, honey, and vanilla until smooth.
3. Spread mixture evenly on prepared baking sheet to 1cm thickness.
4. Sprinkle berries, nuts, chocolate chips, and chia seeds over yogurt.
5. Gently press toppings into yogurt.
6. Freeze for at least 3 h until completely solid.
7. Break into pieces with your hands or knife.
8. Store in freezer in airtight container for up to 1 month.
9. Let sit 2-3 min before eating if very hard.', 'frozen', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1046941224/photo/frozen-yogurt-bark.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=gDwiz_llLXxhrDyDM8X7p2eWVerdCx55K14Sk2fwLlY=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Banana Nice Cream', ARRAY['4 ripe bananas, sliced and frozen', '2-3 tbsp milk of choice', '1 tbsp peanut butter (optional)', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1 tbsp honey or maple syrup (optional)', 'Toppings: chocolate chips, nuts, berries'], '1. Freeze banana slices for at least 2 h.
2. Add frozen bananas to food processor.
3. Process until bananas break down into crumbs.
4. Add milk, peanut butter, vanilla, and sweetener if using.
5. Continue processing until smooth and creamy.
6. Scrape down sides as needed.
7. Serve immediately for soft-serve consistency.
8. Or freeze for 1-2 h for firmer ice cream.
9. Top with desired toppings before serving.', 'frozen', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/921640438/photo/nicecream.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=Q35gRJbd-f9jSla2xfwQGBC2hQeSTq1ODPlz5BfLZzY=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Coconut Popsicles', ARRAY['1 can (400ml) coconut milk', '1/2 cup condensed milk', '1/4 cup granulated sugar', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/4 cup shredded coconut', '2 tbsp lime juice (optional)', '1 tbsp lime zest (optional)'], '1. Whisk coconut milk, condensed milk, and sugar until sugar dissolves.
2. Stir in vanilla extract and shredded coconut.
3. Add lime juice and zest if making lime coconut version.
4. Pour mixture into popsicle molds.
5. Insert popsicle sticks.
6. Freeze for at least 6 h or overnight.
7. To remove, run warm water over molds briefly.
8. Store in freezer for up to 2 months.
9. Let sit 1-2 min before eating if very hard.', 'frozen', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1677513633342-97a36e53a8ae?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8Y29jb251dCUyMHBvcHNpY2xlc3xlbnwwfHwwfHx8MA%3D%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Chocolate Fudge Pops', ARRAY['2 cups whole milk', '1/2 cup heavy cream', '1/2 cup granulated sugar', '1/3 cup unsweetened cocoa powder', '2 tbsp cornstarch', '100g dark chocolate, chopped', '1 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt'], '1. Whisk milk, cream, sugar, cocoa powder, and cornstarch in saucepan.
2. Cook over medium heat, whisking constantly, until thickened.
3. Remove from heat, add chopped chocolate, whisk until melted.
4. Stir in vanilla and salt.
5. Cool mixture to room temperature.
6. Pour into popsicle molds, leaving space at top.
7. Insert sticks and freeze for at least 6 h.
8. Run warm water over molds to remove popsicles.
9. Store in freezer for up to 3 months.', 'frozen', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1591887311330-7de219f362d5?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8Y2hvY29sYXRlJTIwcG9wc2ljbGVzfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Affogato Ice Cream', ARRAY['4 scoops vanilla ice cream', '4 shots hot espresso', '2 tbsp amaretto (optional)', '4 small amaretti cookies', 'Dark chocolate shavings for garnish'], '1. Place one scoop of vanilla ice cream in each serving glass.
2. Prepare hot espresso shots.
3. Add amaretto to espresso if using.
4. Just before serving, pour hot espresso over ice cream.
5. The hot coffee will partially melt the ice cream.
6. Garnish with amaretti cookies and chocolate shavings.
7. Serve immediately with small spoons.
8. Enjoy the contrast of hot and cold.
9. Best consumed within 2-3 min of assembly.', 'frozen', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1696522692156-7340b681c3bb?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8OHx8YWZmb2dhdG98ZW58MHx8MHx8fDA%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'No-Bake Chocolate Oat Cookies', ARRAY['2 cups granulated sugar', '1/2 cup butter', '1/2 cup milk', '1/4 cup unsweetened cocoa powder', '3 cups old-fashioned oats', '1/2 cup peanut butter', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1/2 tsp salt'], '1. Line baking sheets with parchment paper.
2. In a medium saucepan, combine sugar, butter, milk, and cocoa powder.
3. Bring to a rolling boil and boil for 90 seconds.
4. Remove from heat immediately.
5. Quickly stir in peanut butter, vanilla, and salt until smooth.
6. Add oats and mix well until completely coated.
7. Working quickly, drop spoonfuls onto parchment paper.
8. Let cool for 30 min until set.
9. Store in airtight container for up to 1 week.', 'no-bake', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464195085758-89f3e55e821e?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MTV8fGNob2NvbGF0ZSUyMGNoaXAlMjBjb29raWVzfGVufDB8fDB8fHww', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Peanut Butter Balls', ARRAY['1 cup creamy peanut butter', '1/4 cup butter, softened', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1 1/2 cups powdered sugar', '2 cups chocolate chips', '2 tbsp coconut oil', 'Sea salt for sprinkling (optional)'], '1. Mix peanut butter, softened butter, and vanilla until smooth.
2. Gradually add powdered sugar, mixing until dough forms.
3. Roll mixture into walnut-sized balls.
4. Place on baking sheet lined with parchment paper.
5. Chill for 30 min until firm.
6. Melt chocolate chips and coconut oil in microwave, stirring every 30 seconds.
7. Dip each ball in melted chocolate, let excess drip off.
8. Return to parchment paper, sprinkle with sea salt if desired.
9. Chill for 30 min until chocolate sets.', 'no-bake', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/531428399/photo/hand-dipped-chocolate-covered-peanut-butter-creams.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=FSzCts3ZH9JCxOKb5xrcdGqqDDa0Xmo64Ca1UoSTLaY=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Rice Crispy Treats', ARRAY['6 cups rice crispy cereal', '4 cups mini marshmallows', '3 tbsp butter', '1 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt', 'Cooking spray'], '1. Spray 23x33cm pan with cooking spray.
2. Melt butter in large microwave-safe bowl.
3. Add marshmallows to melted butter, microwave in 30-second intervals.
4. Stir until marshmallows are completely melted and smooth.
5. Add vanilla and salt, mix well.
6. Add rice crispy cereal, stir until evenly coated.
7. Press mixture firmly into prepared pan using greased spatula.
8. Let cool for 1 h until set.
9. Cut into squares and serve.', 'no-bake', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/483308876/photo/rice-krispies-treats.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=KivmirDbOT53p7xZpZc3jlFYyXt2NB5Tj4ox3AKq9dw=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Chocolate Truffles', ARRAY['300g dark chocolate, finely chopped', '200ml heavy cream', '2 tbsp butter', '2 tbsp liqueur (optional)', 'Cocoa powder for rolling', 'Chopped nuts for rolling (optional)', 'Shredded coconut for rolling (optional)'], '1. Place chopped chocolate in a large bowl.
2. Heat cream in saucepan until just simmering.
3. Pour hot cream over chocolate, let sit for 2 min.
4. Stir from center outward until smooth and glossy.
5. Stir in butter and liqueur if using.
6. Cover and refrigerate for 2 h until firm.
7. Using a spoon or melon baller, scoop mixture and roll into balls.
8. Roll in cocoa powder, nuts, or coconut.
9. Store in refrigerator for up to 2 weeks.', 'no-bake', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582493255270-b3844e2a63c8?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8Y2hvY29sYXRlJTIwdHJ1ZmZsZXN8ZW58MHx8MHx8fDA%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'No-Bake Cheesecake', ARRAY['Crust: 2 cups graham cracker crumbs', '1/2 cup melted butter', '1/4 cup granulated sugar', 'Filling: 450g cream cheese, softened', '1 cup powdered sugar', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '300ml heavy cream', 'Fresh berries for topping'], '1. Mix graham cracker crumbs, melted butter, and sugar.
2. Press mixture into bottom of 23cm springform pan.
3. Refrigerate while making filling.
4. Beat cream cheese until smooth and fluffy.
5. Add powdered sugar and vanilla, beat until combined.
6. In separate bowl, whip heavy cream to stiff peaks.
7. Gently fold whipped cream into cream cheese mixture.
8. Spread over crust and smooth top.
9. Refrigerate for at least 4 h or overnight.
10. Top with fresh berries before serving.', 'no-bake', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1695088957420-c3b97d1f1138?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8MTF8fGNoZWVzZWNha2V8ZW58MHx8MHx8fDA%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Chocolate Bark', ARRAY['500g dark chocolate, chopped', '1/2 cup dried cranberries', '1/2 cup chopped almonds', '1/4 cup pistachios, chopped', '2 tbsp sea salt flakes', '1/4 cup mini marshmallows (optional)'], '1. Line large baking sheet with parchment paper.
2. Melt chocolate in double boiler or microwave, stirring frequently.
3. Pour melted chocolate onto prepared baking sheet.
4. Spread to about 1cm thickness using offset spatula.
5. Immediately sprinkle cranberries, almonds, pistachios over chocolate.
6. Add marshmallows and sea salt flakes.
7. Gently press toppings into chocolate.
8. Refrigerate for 1 h until completely set.
9. Break into irregular pieces and store in airtight container.', 'no-bake', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/641477300/photo/dark-chocolate-bark.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=ZBNSh00W3M8FaVAlRcfhMlLQwWMP76BOpVpzchj3HNw=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Oreo Balls', ARRAY['1 package (432g) chocolate sandwich cookies', '225g cream cheese, softened', '450g white chocolate, melted', '2 tbsp coconut oil', 'Crushed cookies for decoration (optional)'], '1. Crush cookies in food processor until fine crumbs form.
2. Mix cookie crumbs with softened cream cheese until well combined.
3. Roll mixture into walnut-sized balls.
4. Place on baking sheet lined with parchment paper.
5. Chill for 1 h until firm.
6. Melt white chocolate with coconut oil, stirring until smooth.
7. Dip each ball in melted chocolate, let excess drip off.
8. Return to parchment paper.
9. Sprinkle with crushed cookies if desired.
10. Chill for 1 h until chocolate sets.', 'no-bake', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1321916408/photo/chocolate-cookie-vanilla-ice-creams-in-bowl.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=t6iuSgJUXIZ1Ye10RSCSz758SurjUffVxeZUViTf7LY=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Peanut Butter Fudge', ARRAY['2 cups granulated sugar', '1/2 cup milk', '1/4 cup butter', '1 cup peanut butter', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '3 cups powdered sugar', 'Pinch of salt'], '1. Line 20cm square pan with parchment paper.
2. Combine granulated sugar, milk, and butter in saucepan.
3. Bring to rolling boil, boil for 90 seconds.
4. Remove from heat immediately.
5. Stir in peanut butter and vanilla until smooth.
6. Add powdered sugar and salt, beat until thick.
7. Pour into prepared pan and smooth top.
8. Refrigerate for 2 h until set.
9. Cut into squares and serve.
10. Store covered at room temperature for up to 1 week.', 'no-bake', 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1621245620965-14230f3cc742?w=500&auto=format&fit=crop&q=60&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8ZnVkZ2V8ZW58MHx8MHx8fDA%3D', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Coconut Balls', ARRAY['3 cups shredded coconut', '1 can (397g) sweetened condensed milk', '1 tsp vanilla extract', 'Pinch of salt', '200g dark chocolate, melted (optional)', 'Extra shredded coconut for rolling'], '1. Mix shredded coconut, condensed milk, vanilla, and salt.
2. Stir until mixture holds together.
3. Chill mixture for 30 min to firm up.
4. Roll mixture into walnut-sized balls.
5. Roll balls in extra shredded coconut.
6. Place on baking sheet lined with parchment paper.
7. Chill for 30 min until firm.
8. If desired, dip bottom half in melted chocolate.
9. Let chocolate set before serving.
10. Store in refrigerator for up to 1 week.', 'no-bake', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/465973238/photo/some-coconut-pralines.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=EjLN09nPS0IwuTRYNUj-KtHOKz6z-1hEE7eU7ob77d0=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Cerial Squares', ARRAY['9 cups corn or rice cereal squares', '1 cup chocolate chips', '1/2 cup peanut butter', '1/4 cup butter', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1 1/2 cups powdered sugar'], '1. Place cereal in large bowl.
2. Melt chocolate chips, peanut butter, and butter in microwave.
3. Stir every 30 seconds until smooth.
4. Add vanilla extract and mix well.
5. Pour chocolate mixture over cereal, stir until evenly coated.
6. Place powdered sugar in large plastic bag.
7. Add coated cereal to bag, shake until completely covered.
8. Spread on parchment paper to cool.
9. Store in airtight container for up to 1 week.', 'no-bake', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1505594903/photo/granola-bars-on-the-white-background-top-view.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=q8vHwKzPB2dzP64iKfVNSX590T7kOJ-keIhiiIPOopw=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Classic Apple Turnovers', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '3 large apples, peeled and diced', '1/4 cup brown sugar', '1 tsp cinnamon', '1/4 tsp nutmeg', '2 tbsp cornstarch', '1 egg, beaten', '2 tbsp coarse sugar', '1 tbsp lemon juice'], '1. Preheat oven to 200°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Mix diced apples, brown sugar, cinnamon, nutmeg, cornstarch, and lemon juice.
3. Roll out puff pastry and cut into 6 squares.
4. Place 2 tbsp apple mixture on one half of each square.
5. Fold pastry over filling to form triangles.
6. Seal edges with fork and brush with beaten egg.
7. Sprinkle with coarse sugar.
8. Bake 20-25 min until golden brown.
9. Cool for 10 min before serving.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1150422211/photo/apple-strudel-pastry.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=-nUN-j2BbU1W-SkVvKjV6Uuxk35RXYOq4RgVClaOBok=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Chocolate Croissants', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '100g dark chocolate, chopped', '1 egg, beaten', '2 tbsp milk', '1 tbsp powdered sugar'], '1. Preheat oven to 190°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Roll out puff pastry and cut into 8 triangles.
3. Place chocolate pieces at wide end of each triangle.
4. Roll up from wide end to point, tucking point under.
5. Place on baking sheet, curve into crescent shape.
6. Brush with beaten egg mixed with milk.
7. Bake 15-20 min until golden and puffed.
8. Dust with powdered sugar before serving.
9. Best served warm.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/180824921/photo/fresh-chocolate-croissants-on-a-plate.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=44Uw6NL-hYLCt5pNhVqmFTmlwnnDbUcQC8mfE8WDks8=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Berry Puff Pastry Tart', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '2 cups mixed berries', '1/3 cup granulated sugar', '2 tbsp cornstarch', '1 tbsp lemon juice', '1 egg, beaten', '2 tbsp apricot jam', '1 tbsp water'], '1. Preheat oven to 200°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Roll out pastry into rectangle, place on baking sheet.
3. Score 2cm border around edges, don''t cut through.
4. Prick center area with fork.
5. Mix berries, sugar, cornstarch, and lemon juice.
6. Spread berry mixture inside border.
7. Brush border with beaten egg.
8. Bake 25-30 min until golden and puffed.
9. Heat jam with water, brush over warm tart.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1395084907/photo/rustic-apple-blueberry-and-raspberry-custard-danishes-on-slate-platter.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=uOYM7kq_U543uBKyAa4rHYwlFDM9q-AP8Si5KD591dc=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Cinnamon Sugar Palmiers', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '1/2 cup granulated sugar', '2 tsp ground cinnamon', '1 egg, beaten'], '1. Preheat oven to 200°C. Line baking sheets with parchment.
2. Mix sugar and cinnamon together.
3. Roll out pastry on surface sprinkled with cinnamon sugar.
4. Sprinkle more cinnamon sugar over pastry.
5. Roll both long sides toward center, meeting in middle.
6. Wrap in plastic, chill 30 min.
7. Cut into 1cm thick slices.
8. Place on baking sheet, brush with beaten egg.
9. Bake 15-20 min until golden and caramelized.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/2000284595/photo/palmier-short-for-feuille-de-palmier-palm-tree-leaf-french-hearts-cookies-palmiers-are-made.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=coKQRC5niLBFfUrjQsIDZBEoV51Ozt2ItqbkAbL_YqQ=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Cream Cheese Danish', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '225g cream cheese, softened', '1/4 cup powdered sugar', '1 egg yolk', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1 egg, beaten', 'Fresh berries for topping', 'Powdered sugar for dusting'], '1. Preheat oven to 190°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Beat cream cheese, powdered sugar, egg yolk, and vanilla until smooth.
3. Cut pastry into 9 squares.
4. Make diagonal cuts from corners toward center, leaving center intact.
5. Place 1 tbsp filling in center of each square.
6. Fold alternating points to center, creating pinwheel.
7. Brush with beaten egg.
8. Bake 18-22 min until golden.
9. Top with berries and dust with powdered sugar.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1495083338/photo/top-view-of-two-delicious-cream-cheese-danishes-with-one-half-eaten-on-a-gray-mottled-tabletop.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=pK1aYJknR1PjvqElipsrxMGCTk3EARcKsrJl9fd_XM8=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Nutella Puff Pastry Twists', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '1/2 cup Nutella', '1 egg, beaten', '2 tbsp chopped hazelnuts', '1 tbsp powdered sugar'], '1. Preheat oven to 200°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Roll out pastry into rectangle.
3. Spread Nutella over half the pastry lengthwise.
4. Fold other half over Nutella, press edges to seal.
5. Cut into 12 strips, twist each strip several times.
6. Place on baking sheet, brush with beaten egg.
7. Sprinkle with chopped hazelnuts.
8. Bake 15-18 min until golden and puffed.
9. Dust with powdered sugar when cool.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1491313830/photo/sweden-kanelbullar.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=pzqfbz4n9bZGqZrND17HnAh_BL71aQMjPXugKKizv1I=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Pear and Almond Galette', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '3 ripe pears, sliced thin', '1/4 cup almond flour', '1/4 cup granulated sugar', '2 tbsp butter, softened', '1 egg, beaten', '2 tbsp sliced almonds', '1 tbsp honey'], '1. Preheat oven to 190°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Roll pastry into circle, place on baking sheet.
3. Mix almond flour, sugar, and butter.
4. Spread almond mixture in center, leaving 5cm border.
5. Arrange pear slices over almond mixture.
6. Fold pastry border over filling, pleating as needed.
7. Brush pastry with beaten egg, sprinkle with sliced almonds.
8. Bake 30-35 min until golden.
9. Drizzle with honey before serving.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1158606974/photo/pear-tart.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=M7ks-Ofg41GdHulYdoRDbS3Dz7aB9R9F8u4oRAss4F8=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Strawberry Napoleon', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '2 cups heavy cream', '1/4 cup powdered sugar', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '2 cups fresh strawberries, sliced', '2 tbsp granulated sugar', 'Powdered sugar for dusting'], '1. Preheat oven to 200°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Roll pastry into rectangle, cut into 3 equal strips.
3. Place on baking sheet, prick all over with fork.
4. Bake 15-20 min until golden and crispy. Cool completely.
5. Whip cream, powdered sugar, and vanilla to soft peaks.
6. Toss strawberries with granulated sugar.
7. Layer pastry, cream, and strawberries, ending with pastry.
8. Dust top with powdered sugar.
9. Chill 2 h before serving. Cut with serrated knife.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/165769769/photo/strawberry-mille-feuille-dessert-with-coffee-and-milk.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=IlfK_D1QElMb9eWNWo0g8CdHnCFqQ8clQbVqerM4EII=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Banana Cream Puffs', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '1 ripe banana, mashed', '1 cup heavy cream', '1/4 cup powdered sugar', '1 tsp vanilla extract', '1 egg, beaten', 'Powdered sugar for dusting'], '1. Preheat oven to 200°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Cut pastry into 8 squares.
3. Place on baking sheet, brush with beaten egg.
4. Bake 15-20 min until golden and puffed.
5. Cool completely, then slice horizontally.
6. Whip cream, powdered sugar, and vanilla to soft peaks.
7. Fold mashed banana into whipped cream.
8. Fill puffs with banana cream.
9. Dust with powdered sugar before serving.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/1138250670/photo/homemade-pastry-eclair.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=8CuA2DImROsj9g5yZnjqsiV54Id9f36TtzsSQ0HZKjE=', true, now()),
  ('652e1838-be79-42ee-96e4-9cabfd7a6e40', 'Caramel Apple Strudel', ARRAY['1 sheet frozen puff pastry, thawed', '4 large apples, peeled and sliced', '1/2 cup brown sugar', '1/4 cup caramel sauce', '1 tsp cinnamon', '2 tbsp cornstarch', '1 egg, beaten', '2 tbsp coarse sugar'], '1. Preheat oven to 190°C. Line baking sheet with parchment.
2. Mix apples, brown sugar, caramel sauce, cinnamon, and cornstarch.
3. Roll out pastry into large rectangle.
4. Spread apple mixture along one long edge, leaving border.
5. Roll up pastry tightly, seal seam.
6. Place seam-side down on baking sheet.
7. Brush with beaten egg, sprinkle with coarse sugar.
8. Cut diagonal slashes on top.
9. Bake 35-40 min until golden brown.', 'puff-pastry', 'https://media.istockphoto.com/id/137881018/photo/close-up-of-a-slice-of-apple-strudel-cake.webp?a=1&b=1&s=612x612&w=0&k=20&c=hX41F4wim9R5i0oMiv8QxfvM9RhMrC7NYhdkm-WnbVI=', true, now())
;

